ndation? I'll put scheme \"A\" in certificate. The schema lists scheme in both; certificate-level is enough.\n\nHmm, edition: is \"2007\" the edition? \"R 117/2007\" — yes, OIML R117:2007 is the edition. Include edition: 2007.\n\nNow the characteristics block:\n\ncharacteristics: {\n  \"type_level\": {\n    \"environmental_classes\": {\"value\": \"M3 / E3 / H3\"}\n  },\n  \"config_level\": [\n    {\n      \"attribute\": \"ambient_temperature_range\",\n      \"axis\": \"instrument_used_for_reading_or_recording_of_measurement_results\",\n      \"values\": [\n        {\"condition\": \"default\", \"value\": {\"min\": -25, \"max\": 55}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n        {\"condition\": \"measurement results can be read and/or recorded with an approved instrument\", \"value\": {\"min\": -40, \"max\": 55}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"}\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nWait — rule 5 says config values follow {condition, value, unit_symbol}. OK.\n\nBut hold on: should the ambient temp config be at top level given it belongs to an unidentified part? I'll include it; it's the only place to express it meaningfully. Alternatively inside the first matrix table only. Hmm. I'll include both matrix table and config_level — data preserved twice but that's per rule 4 philosophy (matrix_tables AND model_level).\n\nmatrix_tables[0]:\n{\n  \"name\": \"General characteristics (continuation from previous page — part not identified in this fragment)\",\n  \"columns\": [\"attribute\", \"value\"],\n  \"rows\": [\n    {\"attribute\": \"environmental_classes\", \"value\": \"M3 / E3 / H3\"},\n    {\"attribute\": \"accuracy_class\", \"value\": \"0.3 / 0.5 / 1.0 / 1.5 / 2.5\"},\n    {\"attribute\": \"ambient_temperature_range\", \"value\": \"-25 °C / +55 °C; -40 °C / +55 °C in case the measurement results can be read and/or recorded with an approved instrument\"}\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"General characteristics table whose part attribution is on the preceding page (not included in this fragment).\"\n}\n\nMatrix tables for software — I'll write them all out.\n\nAlso, should the MultiLoad II Table 9 be a matrix_table too? It's captured in components characteristics; fine.\n\nNow assemble the JSON:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R 117/2007-A-NL1-22.02\",\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"project_number\": \"2638810\",\n    \"page_total\": 15,\n    \"member_state\": \"The Netherlands\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"NMi\"\n  },\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Measuring system\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"MultiLoad II\", \"EXL\", \"DIV-2\", \"SMP\"]\n  },\n  \"components\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"Calculating/indicating device\",\n      \"type_designations\": [\"MultiLoad II\"],\n      \"manufacturer\": \"Toptech Systems\",\n      \"characteristics\": {\n        \"type_level\": {\n          \"environmental_classes\": {\"value\": \"M3 / E2\"},\n          \"accuracy_class\": {\"value\": 0.5},\n          \"ambient_temperature_range\": {\"value\": {\"min\": -25, \"max\": 55}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n          \"documentation_folder\": {\"value\": \"TC7311-7\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"type_level\": {\n      \"environmental_classes\": {\"value\": \"M3 / E3 / H3\"}\n    },\n    \"config_level\": [\n      {\n        \"attribute\": \"ambient_temperature_range\",\n        \"axis\": \"approved_instrument_used_for_reading_or_recording_of_measurement_results\",\n        \"values\": [\n          {\"condition\": \"default\", \"value\": {\"min\": -25, \"max\": 55}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n          {\"condition\": \"measurement results can be read and/or recorded with an approved instrument\", \"value\": {\"min\": -40, \"max\": 55}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"}\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"matrix_tables\": [ ... 7 tables ... ],\n  \"recommendation\": {\n    \"id\": \"R117\",\n    \"edition\": 2007,\n    \"accuracy_classes\": [0.3, 0.5, 1.0, 1.5, 2.5]\n  },\n  \"revision_history\"